# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.tp2-full -- GLM-5.3-Flash FULL-SCOPE EXL3 on TWO nodes: TP=2, expert
# parallelism OFF, DFlash2 k=7, per-rank fast-load sidecar.
#
# This is the TP=2 recipe measured on 8 September 2026 -- candidate D: candidate
# C (the full-scope candidate plus the sparse-indexer workspace bound) PLUS the
# vision tower and the two upstream backports.  docs/15-tp2-track.md sections 5,
# 5.9 and 5.10; the vision half is docs/19-vision-at-two-ranks.md.
# KV pool 2,585,714 tokens at max_model_len 1,000,000, C1 59.5 tok/s aggregate
# (64.5 per stream), C8 155.5, fresh prefill 1,413, boot 280 s through the unit,
# gates 10/10 / 12/12 / 8/8, needle-lite 6/6 three times, six vision gates
# including 4 images + 2 videos in one request, and a cached-path equality test
# at 24/24.  Candidate C's rows for comparison: KV 2,692,857, C1 60.1 / 66.0,
# C8 157.7 -- the tower costs 4.0 % of the pool and nothing measurable in speed.
#
# Read env.tp3.example first: the NCCL notes, the block-size reasoning and the
# reasoning-effort note are there and apply unchanged. What follows is only what
# two ranks change, plus the four settings that are not optional here.
#
# ONE COPY PER NODE, derived on that node with sed, NEVER copied between nodes.
# Two lines differ per node (NODE_RANK, HOST_IP) and a copied file that keeps
# the wrong rank produces a cluster where two processes believe they are the
# same rank. The rendezvous completes, the engine starts, the output is wrong.
#
# Placeholders to replace:
#   @NODE_RANK@    0 on the head node, 1 on worker-1
#   @HOST_IP@      this node's own management address
#   @HEAD_IP@      the head node's management address (same on both)
#   @IFACE@        the management network interface name
#   @HOME@         this node's home directory
#   @CKPT@         the full-scope checkpoint directory on this node
#   @DRAFT_TP2@    the DFlash2 drafter directory FOR TWO RANKS (unpadded config)
#
# Consumed by scripts/start-tp2full.sh. Launch order: rank 1, then rank 0.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NODE_RANK=@NODE_RANK@
HOST_IP=@HOST_IP@

# MASTER_ADDR is the MANAGEMENT address of rank 0. A fabric (RoCE) address hangs
# the rendezvous silently; set FABRIC_PREFIX in the environment and the launcher
# refuses one outright.
MASTER_ADDR=@HEAD_IP@
MASTER_PORT=29531
GLOO_IFACE=@IFACE@
TRANSPORT=mesh

NNODES=2
TP_SIZE=2

# OPTIONAL at two ranks, and off in every arm we have measured. The routed
# expert trellis is 2048 wide and 2048/2 = 1024 = 8 x 128, so it tensor-slices
# cleanly; at TP=3 it does not and EP is mandatory. preflight-tp3.py owns this
# arithmetic and will accept either value here. ENABLE_EP=1 at two ranks is
# legal and UNMEASURED -- docs/15 section 6.
ENABLE_EP=0

PORT=8001
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash
QUANTIZATION=exl3
ATTENTION_BACKEND=CUSTOM
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8

# 0.85 is where every TP=2 arm of ours has run, and it is NOT the three-node
# production rung (0.88). Do not copy either number across rank counts: the
# memory left after a fixed cost is not linear in the node count, the ladder has
# never been derived at two ranks, and our first two-node arm recorded 3.5 GB of
# swap on the head during weight load at exactly this rung. docs/15 section 6.
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.85

# Reachable at two ranks with either checkpoint once HAREM_SW_BLOCK_SIZE=256 and
# the launcher's settle gate are both in place. Without them the full-scope
# checkpoint fails its own KV budget gate here -- docs/15 section 5.5.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=1000000
MAX_NUM_SEQS=8
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=2048
ENFORCE_EAGER=0
# 0 == the launcher passes --skip-mm-profiling and the per-request limits rather
# than --language-model-only, which is what turns the vision tower on.  Set it
# to 1 and drop the six vision settings below to serve text only; the tree then
# behaves exactly like candidate C.
LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=0
REASONING_PARSER=deepseek_r1
REASONING_EFFORT=low
CPUSET=5-9,15-19

SPEC_METHOD=dflash
SPEC_TOKENS=7

# Two ranks need no image newer than the loader patch; exl3-zeus:62f53e6 is
# enough. 754421f is used so that both tracks share one image -- and therefore
# one sidecar-invalidation event, since the image tag is part of the manifest.
IMAGE=exl3-zeus:754421f

# No padding sidecar at two ranks: point MODEL_HOST_PATH at the checkpoint
# itself, give MODEL_PATH a plain container path, and leave MODEL_LINK_TARGET
# unset. The DFlash2 drafter's GQA is 32/8, which divides by two, so its 36/9
# TP=3 sidecar is not needed either.
MODEL_HOST_PATH=@CKPT@
MODEL_PATH=/models/glm-5.3-flash-exl3-full
# GIVE THE DRAFTER ITS OWN DIRECTORY AND CHECK ITS CONFIG BEFORE THE DUMP BOOT.
# The three-node track applies its 32/8 -> 36/9 pad by REWRITING config.json
# inside the drafter directory (the original is kept as config.json.orig), so a
# directory shared with a three-node installation carries 9 key-value heads,
# which do not divide by two:
#     qwen3_dflash.py:186  assert self.total_num_kv_heads % tp_size == 0
# four minutes into the boot, after the target model has been read.  Build a
# two-node directory with the unpadded config and a HARD LINK to the same
# weights -- docs/14 section 10.5 has the three commands.  The fast-load
# sidecar identity hashes this config.json, so fixing it later costs a dump.
DRAFT_HOST_PATH=@DRAFT_TP2@
DRAFT_PATH=/models/dflash2-draft

# OVERLAY_DIR is bind-mounted READ-ONLY into the image, so the half of
# patch-indexer-workspace-tp3.py that lands on sparse_attn_indexer_kpool.py
# cannot be written from inside the container. Point this at a COPY of your
# overlay with that half already applied on the host -- run the patch against
# the copy, never against an overlay a running engine is mounting.
OVERLAY_DIR=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/tp2d/overlay
NCCL_MESH_PLUGIN_DIR=@HOME@/nccl-mesh
# Pin CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST to zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash @ 690b7052 (4 Sep 2026),
# 10,950 bytes, sha256 0c4099f3382d6c92700dfb99725025360966fd73032f0ecf32377c0d9e6309c5
# -- only this revision carries the tool-calling fixes, and its clear_thinking
# default is the one both launchers already guard (docs/14 section 9.11 /
# 9.12). Verify with:
#   python3 scripts/verify-chat-template.py "$CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST"
# (script merged from PR #5).
CHAT_TEMPLATE_HOST=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/chat_template.jinja

# The patch directory's file list and the full text of its prelude are hashed
# into the fast-load sidecar's identity (docs/08 section 4), so adding
# patch-indexer-workspace-tp3.py to a tree means a fresh dump boot. Keep the
# candidate-C tree under its own name and its sidecar under its own directory,
# and the previous recipe stays one environment file away.
PRELUDE_DIR=@HOME@/exl3-zeus/tp2d

# HAREM_DISABLE_PERSISTENT_TOPK=1  mandatory on GB10 at any rank count: vLLM's
#     sparse indexer picks a kernel that wants 85 CTAs against 48 SMs and a
#     fallback that wants >=128 KB of shared memory where the part has 101,376.
# NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=8             a plugin property, not a peer-count property.
# CUDA_EXL3_TUNE_CACHE=/cache/tune  warm it before measuring anything (docs/12).
# NCCL_MESH_LINKS_PER_PEER=0       auto. With two cables between the pair, both
#     of them carry ~90 GB across a sweep -- measured at two ranks, docs/15 5.4.
#     Set it to 1 if your pair has one cable; that makes patches/kernel/0005 a
#     no-op.
# HAREM_SW_BLOCK_SIZE=256          MANDATORY IN PRACTICE. Without it the pool is
#     601,562 and a 6,253-token prompt is never scheduled at all. docs/15 4.
# HAREM_DRAFT_KV_DTYPE=fp8         +15.1 % of pool at two ranks, speed and
#     acceptance unchanged, CUDA graphs still capture. docs/15 5.3. (At three
#     ranks the same setting loses the graphs to a wrong support gate,
#     vllm#55581 -- a <=2 % term when the two tracks are compared.)
# HAREM_INDEXER_WS_MODE=bound      +32.14 % of pool on an eager-boot A/B at two
#     ranks, +26.5 % against the previous two-node recipe with the sidecar back.
#     The buffer it bounds is sized from max_model_len alone -- no term in it
#     knows the rank count -- so two ranks pay the same 4.92 GiB against a
#     third of the pool, which is why the gain is three times the three-node
#     one. Unset == upstream sizing byte for byte. docs/15 section 5.9.
#     To see the buffer for yourself, add VLLM_DEBUG_WORKSPACE=1 (an upstream
#     variable, no patch needed): one resize line per rank, 5,036.40 MB without
#     the knob and 513.00 MB with it.
# HAREM_TILELANG_FAILLOUD=1        a silent suppress becomes a named error.
# HAREM_EXL3_FULLSCOPE=1           patch-fullscope-tp2.py: S1 packed mapping,
#     S2 attention dtype, S3 KDA split. REMOVE THIS ONE LINE to serve the
#     routed-experts-only checkpoint instead (and drop --hf-overrides below).
# HAREM_PREFIX_HIT=1               flag ONLY the DFlash2 drafter's KV groups as
#     EAGLE groups.  Unset, nothing is flagged and the coordinator falls back to
#     flagging EVERY group, which drops one whole block off every exact-repeat
#     prefix hit.  At TWO ranks a block is 4,608 tokens and an 8K repeat has
#     only one block of hit to give, so the defect costs the WHOLE hit: 0.0 %
#     against 57.5 % with the knob on, and repeat TTFT 5.60 s against 2.55 s.
#     Measure the granularity yourself (the GCD of the observed hit counts) --
#     it is 3,328 at three ranks and 4,608 here.  docs/15 section 5.10.
# HAREM_KPOOL_TAIL_FIX=1           pass positions through the hybrid
#     attention-metadata path so the K-pool tail's own circular slot mapping
#     runs, and write it in place.  Rank-count independent.
# HAREM_VISION=1 + CUDA_EXL3_PACKED_MAPPING  the vision tower.  NO SPACES in the
#     JSON: EXTRA_ENV is word-split.  docs/19.
EXTRA_ENV="HAREM_PREFIX_HIT=1 HAREM_KPOOL_TAIL_FIX=1 HAREM_DISABLE_PERSISTENT_TOPK=1 NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=8 CUDA_EXL3_TUNE_CACHE=/cache/tune NCCL_MESH_LINKS_PER_PEER=0 NCCL_MESH_MIN_RNR_TIMER=1 NCCL_MESH_PTR_CUDA=1 NCCL_MESH_FLUSH=1 HAREM_SW_BLOCK_SIZE=256 HAREM_DRAFT_KV_DTYPE=fp8 HAREM_TILELANG_FAILLOUD=1 HAREM_EXL3_FULLSCOPE=1 HAREM_INDEXER_WS_MODE=bound HAREM_VISION=1 CUDA_EXL3_PACKED_MAPPING={\"qkv_proj\":[\"q_proj\",\"k_proj\",\"v_proj\"]}"

# SINGLE QUOTES, and NO SPACES inside the JSON: in double quotes the shell eats
# the JSON's own quotes. --hf-overrides is not about padding -- the full-scope
# checkpoint's inlined quantization config carries no tensor_storage, so
# cuda-exl3 has to be pointed at the standalone file. At two ranks that file is
# the checkpoint's own, unrewritten.
# NOTE what is ABSENT: --enable-ep-weight-filter. It needs expert parallelism.
# --mm-encoder-tp-mode data REPLICATES the 0.557 GiB tower on each rank.  It is
# NOT needed at two ranks -- every tower width divides -- and we ship it anyway,
# because dividing means slicing a 6-bit EXL3 tower and nothing in this
# repository has measured that at any rank count.  Decide it BEFORE the dump
# boot: the sidecar stores post-load tensors and the identity does not hash the
# command line.  docs/19 sections 1 and 6.
EXTRA_ARGS='--block-size 256 --safetensors-load-strategy eager --no-enable-flashinfer-autotune --hf-overrides {"quantization_config_file":"/models/glm-5.3-flash-exl3-full/quantization_config.json"} --mm-encoder-tp-mode data --mm-processor-kwargs {"max_pixels":12544000,"max_image_tokens":8000} --limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":4,"video":2} --mm-processor-cache-gb 0'

# Per-rank pre-sliced sidecar. Boot 956 s -> 272 s.
# FASTLOAD_MODE=dump on the FIRST boot only; then change it to load.
# DISK: at two ranks EP is off, so every rank holds HALF of every tensor --
# about 79 GB per rank against 53 GB at three ranks with EP. Check
# "df -h /var/tmp" first: checkpoint plus sidecar needs ~240 GB free per node.
# Give candidate C's sidecar its OWN directory: the same name would overwrite
# the sidecar that is your one-move way back to the previous recipe.
FASTLOAD_DIR=/var/tmp/glm53-exl3-tp2d
FASTLOAD_MODE=load
FASTLOAD_VERIFY=32
FASTLOAD_SHARD_BYTES=2147483648

# Uncomment to prove which modules are EXL3 and which stayed bf16. The
# full-scope candidate prints 203 EXL3 / 113 bf16; the routed-experts-only one
# prints the shared expert, o_proj and lm_head as "unquantized".
# CUDA_EXL3_DEBUG_NAMES=1

# Torch profiler. Off unless set: this vLLM takes it as --profiler-config and
# NOT as VLLM_TORCH_PROFILER_DIR, and with the environment variable alone
# /start_profile answers 404.
# PROFILER_DIR=/cache/prof
